  "decisions": [
    "Three-commit standalone policy/receipt scope; no new split needed before PR009. Existing connector/ingestion exports are read-only dependencies.",
    "Preserve the original measured topology acceptance requirement; documented rate inputs and publication bytes are not actual total operating cost or proof of the cheapest new topology. Missing measurements remain explicit.",
    "Actual retained Census evidence is an unmatched historical negative observation. Route, original expected-content basis and redirect-count unknowns cannot be filled from an approved metadata descriptor. Preserve known safe final host/path and complete rejected-body hash.",
    "Ninety-day raw retention is a default with explicit source-policy overrides, not an unconditional legal floor. Preserve distinct existing GC/audit/lineage obligations.",
    "Pure composer/semantic validator must validate exact underlying contract records, not merely recognize a version. Missing injected validation/identity context must fail closed.",
    "The first downstream connector byte change requires a separately owned additive WP5 successor; do not repin historical WP5. PR010/012 ingestion changes have separate WP4/DB evidence responsibilities.",
    "Reuse prior user authorization for sanitized public-government negative evidence. The fixture copy adds no request or permission to retain aggregate health data.",
    "No R01-R16 cohort or threshold changes. PR009 implementation remains undispatched until PR008 acceptance."
